To be fair, it does crash when loading new areas and saving. But if you remember to save after ever boss fight/Big Daddy fight, you shoudl be fine. So other than that small annoyance, I found this game amazing. Even after ten years, the gameplay still holds up to the standard of todays FPS games, the graphics are great for the time in which the game was created and the story was amazing.
I kinda spoiled a bit of the story for myself by playing Infinite and the Burial At Sea DLC, but that means nada to someone who wouldnt know what the story was about.
So, I reccommend it. And hopefully with the incoming patch, everyone will be able to play without the game crashing and potentially losing an hour of progress;;

Long Version:
TL:DR;
The first 10-15h(YMMV) were fun, but ultimately this is another game that tries to fill Terrarias shoes and fails. My biggest issue with this one is the leveling and monster scaling. Yes the thing that didnt work in Oblivion and was one of the first things fans modded out is in Crea. If i had known i would not have purchased the game in the first place. If you havnt played Terraria go and start with that one. Crea doesnt offer anything new in the 2D sandbox platformer genre.

