Homefront is an FPS, released in 2011 and it's story-line is set in a near future, in America...
The North Korea, somehow gets the hold onto a huge nuclear arsenal - then conquers their south counterparts, and forms the Greater Korean Republic (GKR)... It then continues to conquer/embrace other Asian countries to their ranks, enlarging their army and power...
After creating an massive satellite - for "peace" - they shoot an EMP through the North America that leave it's people completely on the dark... And an invasion from the GKR then follows...
And it's here, two years after this, that we start, in Montrose, Colorado...
You will join a resistance movement that will try to fight back the Korean occupation of the USA.
Note: I didn't find any glitch or problem in the game - like other users have mention...
- Story - It's an imaginative story - and that's what games are for - to entertain us and open up our mind to other possible realites..
